export const evaluatorReports=["## 1. Operational Order (TORC)\n\n**Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is best classified at **3c**.\n\nIts dominant operation is the recursive transformation of a crisis of value and existence into an affirmative existential orientation **without eliminating the underlying instability that produced the crisis**. The death of transcendent guarantees, nihilism, mortality, suffering, recurrence, becoming, solitude, and the instability of inherited values are not merely represented as philosophical themes. They become conditions through which consciousness must reconsider what valuing, willing, identity, and affirmation themselves mean.\n\nSymbolic organization alone is therefore insufficient. Zarathustra's mountain/descent, the three metamorphoses, the tightrope walker, the last man, the Übermensch, self-overcoming, and eternal recurrence operate as parts of a recursive investigation into how consciousness relates to existence after inherited foundations of meaning have become untenable. Under the protocol, Level 3 begins only when that consciousness–reality relation itself becomes the dominant object of inquiry, not merely when symbolism or philosophical complexity appears. \n\nThe highest achieved operation is integration: the work does not restore an external metaphysical guarantee but constructs a mode of orientation in which becoming, suffering, contingency, and recurrence are to be affirmed rather than escaped.\n\n### Boundary analysis: why 3c rather than 3b\n\n**3b is clearly satisfied but insufficient.**\n\nThe existential fracture is fundamental rather than corrective. Zarathustra does not diagnose a problem that better institutions, morality, politics, or social organization could simply repair. The deeper crisis concerns the collapse of externally guaranteed value and the problem of living in a world of becoming, suffering, finitude, and self-overcoming.\n\nThat fits 3b's requirement that contradiction occur in the relation between consciousness and existence itself. \n\nBut the work does not remain in confrontation.\n\nIts major structures progressively construct an orientation:\n\n- **the camel → lion → child** sequence converts submission to inherited value into negation and finally creative affirmation; \n-  the **Übermensch** functions as an orientation toward overcoming rather than restoration of a lost transcendent order; \n- **self-overcoming** makes identity dynamic rather than something to preserve unchanged; \n-  the critique of the **last man** distinguishes mere comfort or pain-avoidance from affirmative existence; \n- **eternal recurrence** intensifies the demand: affirmation must become strong enough to encompass repetition of existence rather than selectively approving only its agreeable portions. \n\nCrucially, this integration does not erase suffering, becoming, death, solitude, or contradiction. The demand is precisely to affirm existence **with** them.\n\nThat directly satisfies the protocol's 3c criterion: contradiction remains operative while consciousness develops a coherent orientation capable of containing it; integration is specifically distinguished from resolution or consolation. \n\nThe completed work also refuses simple triumph. Zarathustra himself repeatedly struggles with disgust, pity, loneliness, discipleship, misunderstanding, and the burden of recurrence. His doctrine is not merely announced once and possessed effortlessly. The teacher must undergo the orientation he teaches.\n\nSo:\n\n**3b:** existential contradiction is exposed.\n\n**3c:** the contradiction becomes incorporated into a structure of affirmation and self-overcoming.\n\nThe latter better explains the whole artifact.\n\n---\n\n## Why not G\n\nThe strongest G candidate would be something like:\n\n**Target:** human valuation and nihilism after the loss of transcendent foundations.\n\n**Candidate structure:** values are not discovered as eternally given but generated through forms of life, willing, overcoming, creation, and valuation; nihilism arises when inherited valuations lose binding force without a capacity for renewed creation.\n\nThat is powerful enough that G deserves serious consideration.\n\nBut the protocol requires more than an encompassing new philosophical picture. A G structure must explain why distinct independently identifiable phenomena take the forms they do, generate nontrivial explanatory consequences across them, and render the lower recursive explanation insufficient. \n\n### Independent Target Test — **Pass**\n\nHuman valuation, nihilism, suffering, aspiration, conformity, resentment, and meaning-making are independently identifiable targets.\n\n### Generative-mechanism test — **Partial / insufficient**\n\nSelf-overcoming and value-creation organize many phenomena, but *Zarathustra* develops them principally through prophetic speech, symbolic transformations, dramatic episodes, oppositions, and existential imperatives.\n\nThe architecture tells us a great deal about **how one should reconceive existence and valuation**, but it does not consistently function as a mechanism explaining why independently constrained classes of phenomena take their particular forms.\n\n### Explanatory-replacement test — **Fail**\n\nThe decisive issue is that **3c remains sufficient**.\n\nThe work can be coherently explained as constructing an integrated existential orientation after the collapse of inherited guarantees. Nothing in the completed artifact requires the stronger claim that it has relocated the explanatory foundation of an independently identifiable domain.\n\nThe protocol explicitly states that when a recursive or integrative account remains sufficient and the proposed higher structure principally provides a new encompassing picture or possibility-space, G must not be assigned. \n\n### Artifact-internal generativity firewall — **Not cleared**\n\nThe novel-philosophical form certainly generates a remarkably interconnected symbolic world. But internally generative symbolism does not itself establish G; the explanatory target must be independently identifiable and its foundation genuinely relocated. \n\nThus the work comes close to **generative appearance**, but the lowest sufficient operation remains **3c**. The protocol explicitly warns that abstraction, symbolic density, philosophical profundity, and interpretive openness are not substitutes for explanatory relocation. \n\n---\n\n# 2. Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\nThe six dimensions below are scored independently and committed before CMS calculation, as required by the protocol. \n\n### RL — Relational Load: **7.4**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 7–8.**\n\nThe artifact sustains numerous consequential nonlocal relations: death of inherited value, nihilism, overcoming, creation, recurrence, temporality, suffering, pity, solitude, teaching, discipleship, embodiment, spirit, herd conformity, higher aspiration, and Zarathustra's own development.\n\nThe symbolic episodes are rarely isolated. The three metamorphoses constrain the meaning of later value-creation; the last man defines a rejected endpoint; Zarathustra's failures qualify his teachings; recurrence radicalizes earlier accounts of affirmation.\n\nThat clearly exceeds modular symbolic accumulation.\n\nMovement toward 8 is substantial, but full dense cross-structural dependency is not established because many speeches and episodes remain meaningfully detachable. The work is deliberately aphoristic and episodic rather than maximally architectonically coupled.\n\n**Principal evidence:** reciprocal relations among nihilism, self-overcoming, value creation, recurrence, and Zarathustra's own enacted development.\n\n**RL: 7.4**\n\n### AD — Abstraction Depth: **8.8**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is fully demonstrated.\n\nThe artifact moves repeatedly across levels:\n\nindividual behavior → morality → value systems → production of values → conditions of valuation → self-transformation → affirmation of existence as becoming.\n\nThe three metamorphoses alone operate simultaneously as images of psychological change, cultural transformation, moral emancipation, and meta-level value creation.\n\nEternal recurrence pushes abstraction further: the problem is no longer simply whether a particular life is desirable but what form of willing could affirm existence without appealing to an external justification for it.\n\nMovement toward 9 is very strong because the work coordinates meta-representational questions about values, identity, time, willing, and meaning. Full 9 is withheld because the relations are often intentionally poetic, polyvalent, and underdetermined rather than maintained through an exceptionally disciplined unified abstraction architecture.\n\n**Principal evidence:** movement from inherited values to the conditions under which valuation itself can be created and affirmed.\n\n**AD: 8.8**\n\n### CD — Constraint Density: **6.8**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 6–7.**\n\nThe work fully reaches 6. Many requirements interact: affirmation must avoid reverting to metaphysical consolation; overcoming cannot terminate in simple negation; the creator must escape both obedience and reactive destruction; recurrence must intensify affirmation rather than merely repeat events; Zarathustra's own behavior must complicate rather than simply exemplify his teaching.\n\nThese create meaningful construction trade-offs.\n\nThere is strong movement toward 7 because the central doctrines must remain compatible across changing rhetorical and symbolic forms.\n\nBut full 7 is withheld. The poetic-prophetic form leaves substantial interpretive and structural latitude, and many speeches could be rearranged, altered, or replaced while preserving the main achievement. The successful construction space is therefore not as tightly narrowed as the work's conceptual richness might suggest.\n\n**Principal evidence:** the requirement to construct affirmative value-creation without restoring the transcendent foundations the artifact has rejected.\n\n**CD: 6.8**\n\n### ID — Inferential Distance: **8.2**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is reached.\n\nSeveral crucial transitions are highly non-routine:\n\n-  from the collapse of inherited values to **creation**, rather than simply skepticism; \n-  from identity to **self-overcoming**; \n-  from suffering as an objection to existence toward suffering as something affirmation must encompass; \n-  from freedom understood as escape from constraint to freedom capable of creating and binding itself; \n-  from ordinary acceptance of life to recurrence as an extreme test of affirmation. \n\nThese require substantial restructuring of familiar moral and existential categories rather than routine deduction.\n\nMovement toward 9 is present but limited. The work often establishes these transitions rhetorically, symbolically, or phenomenologically rather than reconstructing them from a highly constrained evidential problem-space. The conclusions are extraordinarily non-obvious, but claim-radicalness alone cannot establish anchor 9.\n\n**Principal evidence:** conversion of nihilism from an endpoint into a transitional condition for affirmative value creation.\n\n**ID: 8.2**\n\n### IC — Integrative Compression: **8.4**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe full 8 anchor is warranted.\n\nA compact group of structures—**overcoming, creation, affirmation, recurrence, hierarchy of values**—organizes an exceptionally heterogeneous field: morality, psychology, religion, culture, embodiment, temporality, suffering, education, solitude, community, artistic creation, and existential meaning.\n\nThe three metamorphoses provide particularly strong compression: a short symbolic sequence organizes a large developmental architecture while preserving distinctions among obedience, negation, and creation.\n\nLikewise, eternal recurrence compresses many questions about suffering, temporality, value, and affirmation into one extraordinarily economical existential test.\n\nMovement toward 9 is significant, but the artifact does not organize its entire heterogeneous field through one sufficiently explicit and reconstructively complete architecture. Some complexity remains intentionally polyphonic and irreducible.\n\n**Principal evidence:** the economy with which self-overcoming and recurrence organize wide-ranging psychological, moral, cultural, and existential structures.\n\n**IC: 8.4**\n\n### GR — Generalization Reach: **8.1**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nAnchor 8 is just satisfied.\n\nThe central structures transfer across markedly varied cases: morality, religious inheritance, education, artistic creation, personal transformation, social conformity, relationships between teachers and followers, responses to suffering, cultural exhaustion, and existential self-evaluation.\n\nThe transferable invariant is particularly clear in **self-overcoming**: an achieved form becomes something that must itself become material for further transformation rather than a final identity.\n\nThe structure survives substantial contextual change with limited reconstruction.\n\nMovement toward 9 is modest. The artifact's architecture is extraordinarily broad within human existential, psychological, moral, and cultural domains, but it does not demonstrate the same structure across exceptionally distant problem-spaces with the fine fidelity required by 9.\n\n**Principal evidence:** structurally preserved self-overcoming/value-creation architecture across individual, moral, religious, cultural, and existential contexts.\n\n**GR: 8.1**\n\n## Committed profile\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 7.4 / 8.8 / 6.8 / 8.2 / 8.4 / 8.1**\n\n**Profile locked.**\n\nThe protocol requires equal weighting of the six committed scores and CMS calculation only afterward. \n\n7.4+8.8+6.8+8.2+8.4+8.1=47.77.4+8.8+6.8+8.2+8.4+8.1=47.7 47.7/6=7.9547.7/6=7.95 CMS=795\\boxed{\\text{CMS}=795} \n\nThe profile has pronounced **AD–IC–ID–GR strength**: its major achievement lies in abstract reconceptualization, powerful conceptual-symbolic compression, non-routine restructuring of existential problems, and broad transfer across forms of human valuation. **CD is the principal bottleneck**, because its poetic and aphoristic architecture permits considerably more alternative realization than a tightly deductive or formally constrained system.\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 795**\n\nRL: 7.4\n\nAD: 8.8\n\nCD: 6.8\n\nID: 8.2\n\nIC: 8.4\n\nGR: 8.1\n\n**Confidence:** High\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The strongest uncertainty is the **3c/G boundary**: the work's account of nihilism, self-overcoming, and value creation can function as a broad explanatory framework, but the artifact does not demonstrate strongly enough that this framework generates independently constrained explanatory consequences that make integrated recursive consciousness insufficient as the lowest sufficient classification.", "## Operational Order (TORC): **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n***Thus Spoke Zarathustra*** is best classified as **3c**.\n\nIts dominant operation is the construction of an existential orientation capable of affirming a reality from which transcendent guarantees, fixed moral foundations, stable metaphysical purpose, and permanent identity have been withdrawn. The work does not merely diagnose nihilism or dramatize Zarathustra's psychological struggle. It repeatedly turns the problem back upon the consciousness doing the valuing: **how can a being constituted by becoming, suffering, self-overcoming, contingency, and mortality affirm existence without appealing to a world beyond it?**\n\nThe completed trajectory develops an answer through interconnected structures of **self-overcoming, creation of values, the Übermensch, the death of God, will to power, the eternal recurrence, affirmation, solitude/return, and transformation**. Most importantly, the solution does not eliminate becoming, suffering, contradiction, or recurrence. It attempts to transform the subject's *relation* to them.\n\nThat closely matches the protocol's 3c operation: existential fracture remains real, but consciousness develops a coherent orientation capable of containing it rather than merely confronting it. \n\n## Boundary analysis\n\n### Why 3c rather than 3b\n\n**3b is clearly satisfied but insufficient.**\n\nThe underlying fracture is existential rather than merely social or institutional. Removing Zarathustra's prophetic style, biblical parody, animals, mountains, symbolic geography, songs, and dramatic episodes does not remove the central problem: human consciousness confronts impermanence, mortality, groundlessness, suffering, the collapse of inherited value, and its own inability simply to will the past away.\n\nThat passes the **Existential Resistance Principle**. The contradiction exists independently of the artifact's stylistic machinery, satisfying the crucial 3b requirement. \n\nBut the completed artifact does not remain in confrontation.\n\nThe eternal recurrence functions as the hardest integration test. The problem is not merely whether one can tolerate existence once, conditional upon eventual redemption. The envisioned demand is whether consciousness can affirm the recurrence of the whole—suffering, failure, contingency and loss included—without requiring those elements to be erased retrospectively.\n\nLikewise, self-overcoming does not terminate in a permanently perfected self. The structure preserves becoming: overcoming generates further overcoming. Zarathustra himself must repeatedly undergo the doctrine he announces; his failures, disgust, pity, solitude, temptation and return are therefore structurally important rather than incidental imperfections.\n\nThe result is an existential orientation in which contradiction is incorporated rather than abolished. That is exactly what separates 3c from 3b under the protocol. \n\n### Explicit 3c gate\n\nBecause 3c is assigned, every required condition should pass:\n\n**1. Integrated recursion constitutes the dominant operation — PASS.** Zarathustra is not merely a mouthpiece communicating propositions. His ability to *become capable of bearing his own teaching* is part of the operation. Teacher, teaching and existential transformation recursively constrain one another.\n\n**2. Existential contradiction is preserved rather than removed — PASS.** Becoming remains becoming; suffering remains possible; mortality is not canceled; the past cannot literally be changed; value does not regain an external metaphysical guarantor. The affirmative orientation must function under those conditions.\n\n**3. Symbolic consciousness is insufficient — PASS.** Reading the Übermensch, recurrence, mountain, animals, sun, dance, child and transformation merely as an elaborate symbolic system misses why Zarathustra himself repeatedly fails, retreats, returns and changes in relation to what those symbols disclose. The relation between consciousness and the reality it must affirm is operationally central. Under TORC, that is precisely the threshold separating Level 2 from Level 3. \n\n**4. Integration Resistance Principle — PASS.** The work does not qualify because it is optimistic, redemptive or spiritual. Its integration specifically requires retaining what makes affirmation difficult. Eternal recurrence would lose its operative force if pain, contingency and the irreversible past were simply deleted.\n\n**5. A coherent existential orientation rather than emotional resolution — PASS.** The resulting structure is not \"Zarathustra feels better.\" It organizes valuation, temporality, identity, suffering, creation and agency around affirmation and self-overcoming.\n\nAll required 3c conditions are therefore met. \n\n## Why not G\n\nThis is the important upper boundary.\n\nThere is a plausible G reading. The artifact introduces structures—especially genealogy-like value creation, self-overcoming and recurrence—that can reorganize how nihilism, morality and subjectivity are understood.\n\nBut G requires something categorically stronger than profound philosophical reorientation: **explanatory replacement**. A new structure must become the lowest sufficient explanation of an independently identifiable target, rendering the previous explanatory foundation insufficient. For narrative artifacts especially, that relocation must be structurally established by the completed artifact rather than supplied primarily through character belief, authorial pronouncement or external philosophical reconstruction. \n\n*Zarathustra*'s dominant achievement does not require that stronger classification. Its doctrines function most coherently as mutually supporting structures of existential transformation and affirmation. The work does not need to be construed as establishing a new explanatory foundation for an independently constrained domain in order to explain its completed operation.\n\nThe distinction is subtle but decisive:\n\n**3c:** How can consciousness affirm and inhabit becoming without denying its contradictions?\n\n**G:** What newly disclosed structure relocates the explanatory foundation through which an independently identifiable domain must now be understood?\n\nThe first describes *Zarathustra* more completely. Accordingly, under TORC's lowest-sufficient-level rule, the artifact remains **3c**.\n\n---\n\n# Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\nThe profile is determined independently of TORC and before calculating CMS.\n\n| DimensionScoreArtifact-specific evidence |         |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **RL — Relational Load**                 | **8.5** | **8 fully satisfied; substantial movement toward 9.** The work coordinates nihilism, value creation, self-overcoming, Übermensch, will, temporality, recurrence, suffering, pity, solitude, community, embodiment, spirit, resentment, affirmation and Zarathustra's own development. These relations genuinely cross-constrain one another: recurrence tests affirmation; resentment toward time obstructs it; self-overcoming supplies a dynamic model of identity; value creation responds to the collapse of inherited foundations; Zarathustra's failures test the viability of his teaching. It approaches 9 through cross-level interaction among philosophical, psychological, narrative and symbolic structures, but the architecture remains centered on a comparatively compact existential problem rather than achieving complete heterogeneous interdependence. |\n| **AD — Abstraction Depth**               | **9.0** | **9 satisfied.** Concrete experiences repeatedly ascend into structures concerning value, temporality, identity, becoming, agency and affirmation, while those abstractions are recursively tested through Zarathustra's experience. Especially deep is the movement from resentment toward particular suffering → relation to the irreversible past → willing and temporality → recurrence → affirmation of existence as becoming. The work also turns doctrines back upon their speaker, creating a meta-level in which possessing a proposition differs from becoming capable of embodying it. I stop at 9.0 because the architecture is deliberately poetic and polyvalent rather than developing the still more explicit, comprehensive meta-architecture needed for movement toward 10.                                                                                |\n| **CD — Constraint Density**              | **8.0** | **8 satisfied.** The affirmative orientation must avoid several collapses simultaneously: creating values without restoring transcendent foundations; overcoming nihilism without denying suffering; overcoming the self without positing a final static self; affirming becoming without turning it into another metaphysical refuge; rejecting ressentiment while confronting irreversible time; and teaching transformation without reducing it to doctrine. Eternal recurrence dramatically tightens these constraints because affirmation must include rather than selectively edit existence. I stop at 8 because the aphoristic, poetic construction permits substantial interpretive and local structural variation; the viable realization-space is not narrow enough for 9.                                                                                        |\n| **ID — Inferential Distance**            | **8.7** | **8 fully satisfied; close to 9.** The work requires substantial non-routine reconstruction. Its central concepts are not presented as a linear deductive system, and their deeper relations emerge through speeches, reversals, symbols, Zarathustra's failures and transformations. The move from inability to redeem the past to recurrence as a test of unconditional affirmation is particularly inferentially demanding. Movement toward 9 is strong because the architecture must often be reconstructed across distant episodes. I stop below 9 because major relations are repeatedly signaled through explicit speeches and recurring motifs, substantially constraining the interpretive search space.                                                                                                                                                            |\n| **IC — Integrative Compression**         | **9.0** | **9 satisfied.** A remarkably compact architecture—**becoming, overcoming, recurrence and affirmation**—organizes heterogeneous material concerning morality, psychology, temporality, suffering, identity, religion, embodiment, cultural decline and existential orientation. These structures possess genuine reconstructive power: understanding resentment toward becoming, for example, illuminates apparently remote treatments of revenge, pity, metaphysical consolation, the past and recurrence. Compression preserves important distinctions rather than simply assigning everything one label. I stop at 9.0 because considerable symbolic and conceptual machinery remains irreducible to that compact core.                                                                                                                                                   |\n| **GR — Generalization Reach**            | **8.0** | **8 satisfied.** The architecture transfers structurally across moral valuation, personal identity, suffering, temporality, cultural criticism, religious orientation, creativity, interpersonal hierarchy and existential agency. Self-overcoming and affirmation in particular retain their relational structure across quite different cases rather than functioning merely as broad themes. I stop at 8 because demonstrating the 9 anchor would require substantially wider transfer into distant problem-spaces; claiming that Nietzsche's concepts can be applied everywhere would be applicability, not demonstrated generalization.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n\n### Committed profile\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 8.5 / 9.0 / 8.0 / 8.7 / 9.0 / 8.0**\n\n**Profile locked.**\n\nThe architecture shows two principal strengths: **AD and IC**. *Zarathustra* compresses a large existential field through a small number of deeply abstract, recursively related structures. ID is also unusually high because the conceptual architecture is enacted through poetic-narrative transformation rather than delivered as a single explicit argumentative system. CD and GR are the relative bottlenecks: poetic openness enlarges the viable construction space, while broad philosophical applicability cannot substitute for demonstrated transfer.\n\n## CMS\n\nThe protocol requires equal weighting of the six committed scores and mechanical aggregation only after the profile is locked. \n\nCMS=8.5+9.0+8.0+8.7+9.0+8.06×100CMS= \\frac{8.5+9.0+8.0+8.7+9.0+8.0}{6}\\times100 =51.26×100=853.33=\\frac{51.2}{6}\\times100 =853.33 \n\n**CMS = 853**\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 853**\n\nRL: 8.5\n\nAD: 9.0\n\nCD: 8.0\n\nID: 8.7\n\nIC: 9.0\n\nGR: 8.0\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The **3c/G boundary**. The artifact develops concepts capable of radically reorganizing accounts of value, subjectivity and nihilism, but the completed work most securely demonstrates their function as an integrated existential orientation rather than the stronger G requirement of successfully relocating the explanatory foundation of an independently constrained target domain.", "## Operational Order (TORC)\n\n**Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* warrants **3c** because its dominant operation is a recursive investigation of how consciousness can overcome inherited structures of valuation without escaping the conditions of existence that make valuation necessary in the first place. The artifact does substantially more than symbolize philosophical doctrines through mountains, animals, metamorphoses, the tightrope walker, the sun, recurrence, and Zarathustra's journeys. It repeatedly makes the **valuator, teacher, creator, and self-overcomer subject to the same critique and transformation as the values being overcome**.\n\nIts central recursive problem can be stated approximately as follows: if inherited grounds of value lose their authority, consciousness cannot simply occupy a neutral position outside valuation. It must create values; yet the creator is itself historically and psychologically constituted, must overcome itself, and must affirm rather than merely negate the existence from which it creates. Zarathustra's own development enacts this problem rather than merely announcing a solution to it.\n\nThe highest warranted subtype is **3c** because the work develops a positive orientation capable of containing rather than eliminating the resulting contradiction: self-overcoming, creation, affirmation, and ultimately the challenge of eternal recurrence reorganize the relation between becoming, suffering, necessity, and willing. The achievement is not a frictionless reconciliation. The resistant conditions remain; the proposed integration consists precisely in learning to affirm existence without requiring those conditions to disappear.\n\n### Boundary analysis\n\n**Why 3c rather than 3b.** The artifact strongly enters 3b territory. Zarathustra repeatedly fails to stand outside the problems he diagnoses. The teacher needs disciples yet must teach them to abandon him; the creator must destroy inherited values but cannot live permanently through negation; overcoming establishes a new position that itself becomes material for further overcoming; affirmation must include precisely those aspects of existence that provoke resentment against existence.\n\nThose contradictions cannot simply be fixed institutionally or behaviorally.\n\nBut confrontation is not the terminal operation. The text constructs a positive existential architecture around **self-overcoming, value-creation, amor-fati-like affirmation, and eternal recurrence**. The crucial feature of recurrence is not merely cosmological repetition. Operationally, it intensifies the demand that consciousness relate affirmatively to the whole becoming of its existence rather than selectively willing desirable portions while condemning the conditions that produced them.\n\nThis supplies the additional positive evidence required for 3c: the contradiction remains, but an orientation is constructed within which necessity, becoming, suffering, creation, and willing can coexist without requiring metaphysical escape.\n\n**Why not Level 2.** Level 2 is an especially serious alternative because *Zarathustra* is saturated with symbolic architecture. Level 2 permits global metaphor, allegory, thematic patterning, irony, and extreme philosophical sophistication. \n\nYet symbolic organization is insufficient. The three metamorphoses, for example, do not merely symbolize stages. The movement from burden-bearing to negation to creation expresses a recursive structure in which liberation from inherited command is itself insufficient: the consciousness capable of saying “no” must transform again before it can positively legislate.\n\nLikewise, Zarathustra is not a transparent mouthpiece standing outside his doctrine. His solitude, teaching, disgust, pity, temptation, failures, and eventual transformations repeatedly subject the philosophical standpoint itself to its own requirements.\n\nAfter symbolism is accounted for, therefore, a necessary recursive operation remains. The protocol permits Level 3 only under exactly that condition. \n\n**Why not merely 3a.** The work certainly attacks correctable social and cultural structures—herd morality, complacency, certain forms of religion, resentment, nationalism, conventional virtue, and intellectual conformity.\n\nBut abolishing those structures would not resolve its deepest problem. Value-creation, temporality, suffering, mortality, self-division, becoming, and the necessity of overcoming recur at the level of existence itself. The work's solution therefore cannot simply be a better political or moral arrangement.\n\n---\n\n## Explicit G analysis\n\nAlthough I assign 3c, *Zarathustra* presents a plausible G candidate and deserves an explicit boundary test.\n\n**Independent target: PASS.** A target can be identified independently of Nietzschean vocabulary: **how agents generate and sustain valuation and affirmative agency when previously authoritative external or transcendent grounds of value cease to function**.\n\n**Candidate generative structure: PRESENT.** One can formulate a strong candidate:\n\n**valuation is produced by forms of life and willing; established valuations become conditions to which agents become subordinate; overcoming requires transforming the valuating agent itself; consequently, creation is necessarily recursive self-overcoming rather than mere replacement of propositions.**\n\nThis generates substantial consequences across morality, identity, education, resentment, aspiration, suffering, and interpersonal hierarchy.\n\n**Generative mechanism versus explanatory schema: PARTIAL.** The protocol requires G to explain why independently identifiable target phenomena take their forms, rather than primarily arranging them inside a powerful new picture. \n\nHere the evidence is mixed. The self-overcoming architecture explains important patterns, but *Zarathustra*'s dominant achievement remains dramatic-recursive enactment of an existential transformation. Concepts such as will to power, Übermensch, and recurrence are not developed here into a sufficiently constrained explanatory mechanism that makes the recursive account operationally inadequate.\n\n**Explanatory replacement: FAIL.** G requires lower-order explanation to become insufficient.  It does not. 3c explains the completed artifact economically: recursive destabilization of inherited valuation followed by construction and testing of an existential orientation capable of affirming the resistant conditions uncovered by that destabilization.\n\n**Independent-constraint test: NOT FULLY ESTABLISHED.** The artifact's philosophical structures are constrained by recognizable phenomena—resentment, conformity, self-division, suffering, aspiration, dependency, valuation—but its strongest ontological formulations are not derived tightly enough from those independent constraints to force explanatory relocation.\n\nTherefore **G is not warranted**. The protocol explicitly forbids turning philosophical magnitude, universality, novelty, or a large explanatory architecture into G without successful explanatory relocation. \n\n---\n\n# Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\n### RL — Relational Load: **8.3**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is established. The work coordinates value, nihilism, overcoming, creation, destruction, teaching, discipleship, solitude, community, pity, resentment, embodiment, suffering, temporality, willing, recurrence, affirmation, death, and identity.\n\nCrucially, these relations constrain one another. Creation depends on overcoming; overcoming threatens to become endless negation; teaching produces dependence that contradicts the goal of independence; affirmation is tested by suffering; recurrence radicalizes affirmation; Zarathustra's own development changes the meaning of doctrines he previously announces.\n\nThere is meaningful movement toward 9 because psychological, ethical, existential, pedagogical, temporal, and narrative structures become mutually consequential.\n\nI stop below 9 because the architecture remains substantially modular and aphoristic. Many episodes and speeches can retain considerable local intelligibility without requiring simultaneous reconstruction of the entire network.\n\n**Principal evidence:** nonlocal interaction among self-overcoming, value creation, teaching, affirmation, temporality, suffering, and Zarathustra's own recursive development.\n\n### AD — Abstraction Depth: **8.8**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is clearly satisfied: substantial conceptual distance is traversed while preserving strong structural correspondence.\n\nThe text repeatedly moves from concrete image → psychological relation → structure of valuation → structure of self-transformation → existential relation to becoming. Camel/lion/child, ascent/descent, giving/receiving, sickness/recovery, noon/midnight, and recurrence operate across several representational levels without functioning merely as detachable allegories.\n\nMovement toward 9 is particularly strong because **self-overcoming itself becomes meta-structural**: not merely one value among others, but a principle according to which valuating structures and the consciousness holding them become objects of further transformation.\n\nI stop just below 9 because the highest abstractions are deliberately polyvalent. Their relations remain less systematically disciplined than the complete 9 anchor's “exceptional abstraction architecture” requires. The protocol explicitly prevents philosophical obscurity or apparent profundity from substituting for disciplined invariant preservation. \n\n**Principal evidence:** recursive ascent from particular values to valuation, from valuation to the valuating self, and from the valuating self to self-overcoming and affirmation as meta-structures.\n\n### CD — Constraint Density: **7.5**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 7–8.**\n\nThe 7 anchor is established. Numerous requirements interact: Zarathustra must overcome inherited values without becoming merely reactive to them; create without converting creation into a new external command; teach without producing permanent followers; affirm suffering without merely glorifying suffering; affirm becoming without appealing to a static transcendent world; and overcome himself without positing a final static self.\n\nThese requirements create genuine trade-offs.\n\nThere is movement toward 8 because narrative, rhetorical, psychological, ethical, and philosophical constraints intersect. Zarathustra's behavior must also test rather than simply illustrate his teachings.\n\nBut the complete 8 anchor is not demonstrated. The artifact's poetic form permits considerable multiplicity, contradiction, reformulation, and local independence. Alternative constructions could preserve much of its central achievement.\n\nThe protocol requires actual solution-space compression, not simply intellectual difficulty. \n\n**Principal evidence:** tightly interacting requirements governing non-reactive creation, self-overcoming, teaching, affirmation, and resistance to transcendental escape.\n\n### ID — Inferential Distance: **8.2**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is established: several highly non-obvious restructurings occur without routine routes. \n\nMajor examples include the transition from loss of transcendent authority to the problem of *creating* rather than merely discovering values; from overcoming external authority to overcoming the self that performed the overcoming; from liberation through negation to the requirement of affirmative creation; and from accepting individual events to testing whether one could affirm their necessary embeddedness in the whole of one's existence.\n\nThe child following the lion is a particularly compressed inferential restructuring: freedom-from is discovered to be insufficient for freedom-to.\n\nThere is movement toward 9 because the problem-space permits many plausible responses that do not yield this architecture.\n\nI stop at 8.2 because several decisive transitions are poetically asserted or dramatized rather than inferentially compelled. Under the protocol, magnitude of leap cannot substitute for successful inferential reconstruction.\n\n**Principal evidence:** non-routine transformation of nihilism → creation, liberation → self-overcoming, and acceptance → comprehensive affirmation.\n\n### IC — Integrative Compression: **8.5**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe 8 anchor is strongly established.\n\nA relatively compact family of relations—**overcoming, creation, affirmation, recurrence, resentment, embodiment, giving, and becoming**—organizes an unusually heterogeneous body of psychological, ethical, existential, religious, pedagogical, and narrative material.\n\nThe compression is especially powerful because the same structure reconstructs apparent oppositions. Destruction and creation become phases of one process; independence and discipleship become recursively connected; suffering and affirmation interact; solitude and giving become mutually necessary; overcoming oneself becomes continuous with overcoming inherited valuation.\n\nMovement toward 9 is substantial.\n\nI stop at 8.5 because the work deliberately resists reduction to one compact explanatory architecture. Its symbolic and conceptual plurality carries genuine irreducible information. Further compression would begin deleting distinctions rather than economically organizing them.\n\n**Principal evidence:** a small family of recursive existential structures renders a large range of otherwise disparate speeches, symbols, psychological states, and narrative events mutually intelligible.\n\n### GR — Generalization Reach: **7.5**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 7–8.**\n\nThe 7 anchor is satisfied.\n\nA transferable structure can be identified:\n\n**inherit a governing valuation → become capable of negating it → discover that negation remains dependent on what it rejects → transform the valuating agent → create a positive orientation → subject that orientation itself to further overcoming.**\n\nThis architecture transfers with strong fidelity across morality, identity, education, artistic creation, religious inheritance, interpersonal dependence, psychological development, and cultural criticism.\n\nA second structure—affirming an outcome together with the conditions inseparable from producing it—also transfers across multiple existential cases.\n\nThere is meaningful movement toward 8, but the protocol's firewall matters. Broad applicability to human life is not automatically structural transfer across markedly heterogeneous problem-spaces. \n\nThe demonstrated reach remains concentrated primarily within human psychological, ethical, existential, and cultural transformation.\n\n**Principal evidence:** high-fidelity transfer of the self-overcoming architecture across substantially different forms of valuation and identity formation, with limited demonstrated domain distance beyond human/existential problems.\n\n---\n\n## Committed Six-Dimensional Architecture\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR**\n\n**8.3 / 8.8 / 7.5 / 8.2 / 8.5 / 7.5**\n\nProfile locked before calculating CMS, as required by the protocol. \n\nCMS=8.3+8.8+7.5+8.2+8.5+7.56×100CMS= \\frac{8.3+8.8+7.5+8.2+8.5+7.5}{6}\\times100 =48.86×100=813.33=\\frac{48.8}{6}\\times100 =813.33 \n\n**CMS = 813**, using the protocol's required nearest-whole-integer rounding. \n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 813**\n\nRL: 8.3\n\nAD: 8.8\n\nCD: 7.5\n\nID: 8.2\n\nIC: 8.5\n\nGR: 7.5\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The 3c/G boundary. The self-overcoming architecture has genuine explanatory power beyond Zarathustra's individual existential development and generates consequences across several independently recognizable phenomena of valuation and agency. The limiting issue is whether *Thus Spoke Zarathustra* successfully establishes that architecture as a new explanatory foundation for those phenomena, or primarily realizes it as a recursive-integrative existential orientation. On the artifact's demonstrated operation, the latter is better supported.", "## 1. Operational Order (TORC)\n\n**Classification: Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is best classified at **3c** because its dominant operation is not merely symbolic prophecy, aphoristic philosophy, or existential fracture. The work repeatedly stages the breakdown of inherited value structures, the instability of the self, the burden of recurrence, the danger of ressentiment and nihilism, and the difficulty of becoming capable of affirming life—then tries to integrate those fractures into a coherent existential orientation centered on self-overcoming, creation of values, affirmation, and eventually the capacity to will recurrence rather than merely endure existence.\n\nThe decisive point is that contradiction is **preserved rather than erased**. Suffering, finitude, conflict, becoming, and instability are not removed by the artifact's solution. They become the very material through which a higher orientation is to be constituted. That matches the protocol's 3c structure: contradiction remains operative, yet consciousness develops an orientation capable of containing it. \n\n### Boundary analysis\n\n**Why 3c rather than 3b.** A 3b reading is initially very strong. The artifact confronts death, nihilism, self-division, failed communication, loneliness, recurrence, and the collapse of inherited metaphysical guarantees. Zarathustra repeatedly encounters a world in which ordinary structures of meaning are no longer sufficient.\n\nBut the work does not remain in confrontation.\n\nIts dominant trajectory is toward **affirmative integration**: overcoming reactive valuation, creating rather than merely inheriting values, learning to affirm becoming, transforming suffering into something incorporable into a larger form of life, and ultimately approaching an orientation in which even recurrence can be willed.\n\nThat is exactly the additional operation separating 3c from 3b. The protocol requires that 3c integrate existential contradiction without pretending to abolish it. \n\nThe Integration Resistance Principle is therefore satisfied. The work does not merely offer optimism, consolation, reconciliation, or closure. Its “yes” to existence only has force because the negative remains real: suffering is not denied, becoming is not stabilized into permanent being, and contradiction is not converted into a painless resolution.\n\n**Why not Level 2.** Symbolism is extraordinarily dense—mountains, animals, sun, abyss, child, camel/lion, dancing, bridges, circles, heights—but symbolic organization alone does not explain the artifact. Those symbols repeatedly serve a recursive transformation in the relation between consciousness, valuation, and existence. The protocol explicitly requires advancement beyond Level 2 only when symbolic organization is insufficient and a recursive operation remains after symbolism has been accounted for. \n\nHere, it does.\n\n---\n\n## Why not G\n\nThis is the critical upper boundary.\n\nA plausible G reading would identify the independent target as **human valuation and nihilism** and claim that the work relocates explanation from objective or inherited values to value-creation rooted in life, perspective, overcoming, and force.\n\nThat is genuinely close to the G threshold.\n\nBut the protocol's G gate is stricter than conceptual radicality. G requires a newly disclosed generative structure that explains why otherwise distinct target phenomena take the forms they do and renders lower-order explanation insufficient. It must be more than a powerful redescription or philosophical reorientation. \n\nThe artifact does not establish a sufficiently constrained generative mechanism for the independently identifiable target. Concepts such as will to power, overcoming, decadence, ressentiment, value creation, and recurrence supply a powerful interpretive architecture, but in *Zarathustra* they operate predominantly through prophetic, symbolic, existential, and perspectival reorganization rather than through a demonstratively generative explanatory mechanism.\n\nPut differently: the work **transforms how existence may be inhabited and valued more decisively than it transforms what explains an independently constrained domain**.\n\nUnder the protocol's categorical clarification, that remains Level 3 rather than G, regardless of depth, originality, or radicality. \n\nSo the highest warranted classification is **3c**.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\nThe dimensional profile is scored independently of the TORC classification. The protocol forbids TORC leakage and requires commitment of the six scores before CMS calculation. \n\n### RL — Relational Load: **8.4**\n\n**Anchor interval: 8–9.**\n\nThe work coordinates numerous consequential relations among nihilism, morality, self-overcoming, resentment, pity, solitude, community, recurrence, time, affirmation, creation, destruction, embodiment, language, teaching, discipleship, and transformation of the self.\n\nThese relations are strongly nonlocal. Earlier formulations are repeatedly revised by later encounters; Zarathustra's teaching is inseparable from his failures to communicate it; self-overcoming is connected to both value creation and the overcoming of the teacher's own attachment to disciples and doctrine.\n\nThat fully satisfies RL8: remote relations materially constrain one another and simultaneous coordination is central. \n\nMovement toward 9 is significant because psychological, ethical, metaphysical, rhetorical, and existential levels remain mutually consequential. I stop below 9 because the relational field, though dense, is less globally interdependent than a system in which virtually every major component requires continuous coordination with the whole.\n\n**Principal evidence:** recurrence, affirmation, self-overcoming, value creation, and Zarathustra's own developmental failures mutually reinterpret one another across the work.\n\n### AD — Abstraction Depth: **9.0**\n\n**Anchor: 9 fully satisfied.**\n\nThe artifact operates through exceptionally deep abstraction. Concrete images and episodes repeatedly become vehicles for higher-order structures involving valuation, becoming, identity, temporality, recurrence, power, perspective, and the possibility of affirming existence without appeal to transcendent guarantees.\n\nThe abstraction is not merely thematic. Structures such as camel → lion → child encode transformations in the relation between inherited norm, negation, and creation. The eternal recurrence transforms a cosmological or hypothetical proposition into a test of one's entire orientation toward existence.\n\nThat satisfies the protocol's 9-anchor: very deep invariant/meta-level structures organize broad heterogeneous material while preserving relational discipline. \n\nI stop at 9.0 because the highest abstractions remain intentionally polyvalent and poetic. They retain enormous structural power but are less tightly formalized than would justify stronger movement toward the ceiling.\n\n**Principal evidence:** repeated ascent from concrete image and psychological disposition to general structures of valuation, temporality, selfhood, and affirmation.\n\n### CD — Constraint Density: **8.0**\n\n**Anchor: 8 fully satisfied.**\n\nThe artifact must sustain many interacting requirements simultaneously: Zarathustra must be teacher and failed teacher; affirmation cannot collapse into naïve optimism; self-overcoming must preserve conflict rather than merely resolve it; value creation must avoid becoming another fixed dogma; recurrence must function existentially without being reducible to a simple cosmological claim; prophetic language must remain philosophically productive without becoming merely ornamental.\n\nThese are heterogeneous constraints across narrative, symbolic, philosophical, psychological, and rhetorical levels.\n\nThat meets CD8: local optimization regularly threatens other functions. \n\nI do not move substantially toward 9 because many local episodes, speeches, images, and narrative transitions could be altered while preserving the dominant operation. The protocol cautions against treating sheer narrative or symbolic richness as proof of extreme solution-space compression. \n\n**Principal evidence:** the work's need to keep affirmation, suffering, creation, negation, teaching, solitude, and recurrence in productive tension.\n\n### ID — Inferential Distance: **8.4**\n\n**Anchor interval: 8–9.**\n\nThe work makes several deep non-routine transitions: from the collapse of inherited values to the need for value creation; from selfhood as something possessed to selfhood as something overcome and produced; from suffering as objection to existence to suffering as potentially incorporable into affirmation; and from recurrence as repetition to recurrence as an existential measure of whether one can will one's life.\n\nThese are highly non-obvious restructurings with no routine path, satisfying ID8. \n\nThere is real movement toward 9 because many plausible alternatives remain and the text often has to transform the problem-space itself before its conclusions become intelligible.\n\nI stop at 8.4 because several decisive transitions are enacted rhetorically, poetically, or performatively rather than fully inferentially reconstructed. Radicality of conclusion cannot substitute for supported inferential distance.\n\n**Principal evidence:** transformation of nihilism, suffering, recurrence, and selfhood into elements of an affirmative existential architecture.\n\n### IC — Integrative Compression: **8.7**\n\n**Anchor interval: 8–9.**\n\nA relatively compact architecture—**self-overcoming, creation of values, affirmation of becoming, and recurrence**—organizes an unusually heterogeneous field: morality, psychology, religion, temporality, embodiment, suffering, culture, pedagogy, solitude, sociality, resentment, and existential meaning.\n\nThe same small cluster of structures allows distant parts of the work to become mutually intelligible without simply collapsing their differences.\n\nThis comfortably satisfies IC8 and approaches 9. \n\nI stop below 9 because some of the apparent compression is achieved through extremely capacious concepts whose boundaries remain intentionally elastic. The protocol warns that universal vocabulary alone is not integrative compression. \n\n**Principal evidence:** the ability of self-overcoming and affirmation to organize ethical, psychological, temporal, cultural, and existential structures simultaneously.\n\n### GR — Generalization Reach: **8.0**\n\n**Anchor: 8 fully satisfied.**\n\nThe transferable structure is clear: inherited forms of valuation can become life-denying; negation may be necessary but insufficient; agency can be transformed through self-overcoming; and a more robust orientation emerges when one becomes capable of creating and affirming rather than merely reacting.\n\nThis structure transfers across moral life, personal identity, education, culture, suffering, social relationships, religion, creativity, temporality, and existential orientation.\n\nThat meets GR8's requirement for substantial transfer across markedly heterogeneous cases with limited reconstruction. \n\nI stop at 8.0 because the protocol's applicability firewall matters. Broad relevance to human existence is not equivalent to demonstrated transfer across exceptionally distant problem-spaces. \n\n**Principal evidence:** preservation of the same overcoming/affirmation architecture across ethical, psychological, cultural, religious, and existential domains.\n\n### Committed profile\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 8.4 / 9.0 / 8.0 / 8.4 / 8.7 / 8.0**\n\nProfile locked.\n\nCMS is mechanically calculated from the committed six-dimensional profile, with equal weighting. \n\n8.4+9.0+8.0+8.4+8.7+8.06=8.4166…\\frac{8.4+9.0+8.0+8.4+8.7+8.0}{6} =8.4166\\ldots \n\n**CMS = 842**\n\nThe profile is strongest in **abstraction depth and integrative compression**. Its main limiting factor is not philosophical depth but the degree of formal constraint and explanatory mechanism: the artifact integrates a very large existential field through powerful recurring structures, but those structures remain more poetic, perspectival, and interpretive than maximally constrained.\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 842**\n\nRL: 8.4\n\nAD: 9.0\n\nCD: 8.0\n\nID: 8.4\n\nIC: 8.7\n\nGR: 8.0\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The 3c/G boundary. The artifact strongly relocates valuation away from inherited/transcendent foundations toward creation, overcoming, and affirmation, but I judge that this remains primarily an integrated recursive existential reorientation rather than a sufficiently constrained generative explanation of an independently identifiable target domain.", "## 1. Operational Order (TORC)\n\n# **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\nFriedrich Nietzsche's *Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is best classified as **3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**.\n\nIts dominant operation is not adequately captured by its extraordinary symbolic system—Zarathustra's mountain and descent, sun, eagle and serpent, tightrope, child, lion, camel, sea, abyss, dance, noon, recurrence, and overman. Those structures matter enormously, but symbolic interpretation alone does not explain the completed artifact.\n\nThe deeper operation concerns **how a consciousness can orient itself after inherited structures of value, metaphysical guarantee, purpose, and moral authority have ceased to provide that orientation**. Crucially, the work does not merely diagnose this condition. Zarathustra's own teaching, identity, valuation, solitude, disgust, pity, aspiration, and relation to recurrence are repeatedly subjected to the same transformative pressure.\n\nIts central movement can be represented approximately as:\n\n**collapse of inherited valuation → danger of nihilistic/disintegrative existence → creation of values → recursive confrontation with the creator's own residual attachments and negations → affirmation tested against recurrence → an existential orientation capable of affirming becoming rather than requiring its metaphysical correction.**\n\nThe final step warrants **3c rather than 3b**. The artifact does not eliminate contradiction, suffering, temporality, loss, contingency, or becoming. Its attempted integration consists precisely in constructing an orientation that can contain them without requiring their abolition.\n\nUnder the protocol, Level 3 begins when representation, interpretation, orientation, or the conditions through which reality becomes intelligible become themselves objects of inquiry.  *Zarathustra* does this globally.\n\n---\n\n## Boundary analysis\n\n### Why 3c rather than Level 2\n\nLevel 2 initially looks plausible because the book is intensely symbolic. Indeed, reading the overman, eternal recurrence, the three metamorphoses, Zarathustra's descent, the tightrope walker, noon, dance, gravity, and the child symbolically explains a tremendous amount.\n\nBut the protocol's Symbolic Ceiling Principle requires asking whether, **after the symbolic organization has been accounted for, a distinct recursive operation remains**. \n\nIt does.\n\nZarathustra does not simply deliver a symbolic doctrine. The work progressively tests the **position from which such a doctrine can be lived and affirmed**. Zarathustra himself repeatedly becomes the object of the inquiry. The teacher must overcome his need for disciples; the creator must confront his own reactive residues; the affirmative prophet must encounter disgust; the advocate of overcoming must overcome himself; and the doctrine of recurrence becomes inseparable from whether Zarathustra can actually will existence under its demand.\n\nThis produces genuine recursion:\n\n**valuation → consciousness producing valuation → motives and attachments of that valuating consciousness → whether the evaluator can affirm the conditions under which valuation itself occurs.**\n\nThus symbolism is indispensable but insufficient. The protocol requires exactly this for advancement: symbolic organization must be insufficient, recursive operation positively present, and that operation globally governing. \n\nAll three conditions are satisfied.\n\n### Why 3c rather than 3a\n\nThe book contains a powerful corrective operation. Christianity, otherworldly metaphysics, conventional morality, pity, ressentiment-like valuation, nationalism, egalitarian complacency, the \"last man,\" and various cultural ideals are attacked as inadequate orientations.\n\nIf the artifact merely diagnosed those inherited structures and proposed superior values, **3a** could suffice.\n\nBut its problem cannot ultimately be solved by correcting a defective doctrine or institution. Once transcendent guarantees collapse, consciousness confronts a deeper question: **how can finite, temporal, suffering existence be affirmed without appealing to a world or standard outside becoming?**\n\nThe correction therefore opens into an existential problem rather than completing it.\n\n### Why 3c rather than 3b\n\nThis is the decisive boundary.\n\n*Zarathustra* unquestionably contains 3b-level fracture. The creator must destroy inherited values yet cannot create from nowhere; consciousness seeks affirmation while confronting suffering and disgust; the will encounters the irreversibility of \"it was\"; overcoming itself risks becoming another form of negation; Zarathustra must confront what in existence he finds hardest to affirm.\n\nIf the artifact terminated in that confrontation, 3b would be sufficient.\n\nBut it performs an additional operation: **affirmation becomes a mode of integration**.\n\nEternal recurrence is crucial here regardless of whether it is interpreted cosmologically, existentially, or as a test of affirmation. Its operational role is to intensify the problem to its limit: can existence be affirmed not selectively—not merely its pleasures, achievements, or desired future—but in such a way that its temporality, suffering, contingency, repetition, and irrevocability no longer require metaphysical cancellation?\n\nThe transformation of the spirit culminating in the **child** similarly does not mean returning to innocence by forgetting negation. The child comes *after* camel and lion: affirmation incorporates burden-bearing and negation rather than simply preceding them.\n\nLikewise, Zarathustra's increasingly affirmative relation to dance, laughter, becoming, recurrence, and his own task provides a coherent orientation emerging through rather than around the contradiction.\n\nThis meets the protocol's distinction: 3c **preserves the contradiction while performing the additional operation of integrating it into a coherent existential orientation without simply erasing it**. \n\nThe integration is not a systematic philosophical resolution. It does not need to be. What matters operationally is that the completed artifact transforms confrontation into a livable affirmative orientation.\n\n---\n\n## Why not G?\n\nThis is a serious boundary because *Zarathustra* contains ideas with substantial explanatory power: genealogy-like accounts of valuation, self-overcoming, will to power, nihilism, eternal recurrence, perspectival structures, and the overman.\n\nBut TORC explicitly forbids moving from philosophical profundity or large explanatory structures directly to G. A work about reality, meaning, or consciousness is not automatically generative, and universal claims do not by themselves demonstrate generative disclosure. \n\nApplying the relevant tests:\n\n**Independent Target Test — PASS/PARTIAL.** Independently identifiable targets exist: nihilistic disorientation, value conflict, reactive valuation, self-division, temporality, suffering, aspiration, and the psychological dynamics of overcoming.\n\n**Candidate generative mechanisms — PRESENT.** Self-overcoming and the dynamics through which valuation arises from forms of life have genuine explanatory potential.\n\n**Generative Mechanism Test — PARTIAL.** The work sometimes explains phenomena through these structures, but *Zarathustra* characteristically operates through dramatization, aphorism, symbolic transformation, exhortation, recursive testing, and existential enactment rather than sustained generative derivation.\n\n**Explanatory Replacement — NOT SUFFICIENTLY DEMONSTRATED.** The artifact transforms how its problems are experienced and interpreted, but it does not globally establish a new explanatory mechanism that makes a previous explanatory foundation inadequate in the strong G sense.\n\n**Explanatory-Object Firewall — PASS/PARTIAL.** Many targets are independently accessible, but some of the central architecture—especially the overman and recurrence in their strongest forms—is partly constituted through the artifact's own philosophical-symbolic framework.\n\n**Projection Independence — decisive caution.** It would be easy to import a systematic Nietzschean philosophy assembled from *Beyond Good and Evil*, *On the Genealogy of Morality*, notebooks, or later scholarship and thereby make *Zarathustra* look more systematically generative than this completed artifact itself demonstrates. The protocol forbids the evaluator from supplying the higher operation through external theory. \n\n**Lower-order insufficiency — FAIL for G.** Most importantly, 3c already explains the completed artifact's dominant achievement: recursive transformation culminating in an affirmative existential orientation.\n\nTherefore the classification terminates at **3c**.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\n### **RL — Relational Load: 8.0**\n\nThe work maintains a large network of consequential relationships among nihilism, value creation, overcoming, recurrence, temporality, will, body, spirit, solitude, teaching, discipleship, pity, revenge, suffering, joy, affirmation, death, humanity, and the overman.\n\nIts symbolism participates in the same network rather than merely decorating it. Height/depth, ascent/descent, heaviness/dance, noon/night, animal/human/overman, destruction/creation, and departure/return continually modify one another.\n\nLong-range relations matter substantially: teachings introduced early acquire altered significance after Zarathustra himself undergoes the conditions they describe.\n\nThis reaches **8: dense relational architecture**.\n\nI stop at 8.0 because the work is deliberately episodic and aphoristic. Many speeches possess substantial local autonomy, so the whole is less tightly cross-dependent than an architecture in which altering one remote component systematically destabilizes most others.\n\n**Principal evidence:** reciprocal dependence among value destruction, creation, self-overcoming, recurrence, affirmation, and Zarathustra's own development.\n\n### **AD — Abstraction Depth: 8.6**\n\nThe artifact traverses substantial abstraction levels:\n\n**particular moral practice → type of valuation → conditions generating values → creator of values → self-overcoming of the creator → affirmation of the temporal/existential conditions within which creation itself occurs.**\n\nLikewise, concrete experiences of disgust, revenge, suffering, joy, loneliness, and aspiration are progressively related to deeper structures of temporality, valuation, becoming, and affirmation.\n\nThe symbolic architecture often carries these abstractions while preserving their relations. Camel → lion → child, for instance, is not simply three images but a compressed meta-structure concerning incorporation, negation, and creation.\n\nThis fully establishes **8-level deep constrained abstraction** and moves strongly toward 9.\n\nI stop below 9 because the artifact deliberately refuses complete systematic articulation. Its highest abstractions maintain productive ambiguity, and several central concepts permit multiple structurally plausible relations rather than forming one exceptionally disciplined meta-architecture.\n\n**Principal evidence:** movement from criticism of particular values to inquiry into valuation itself and ultimately into the existential conditions under which value creation can be affirmed.\n\n### **CD — Constraint Density: 7.5**\n\nThe artifact must coordinate substantial interacting requirements.\n\nAffirmation cannot simply restore the metaphysical guarantees the work attacks. Value creation cannot merely reproduce inherited obedience. Self-overcoming cannot terminate in static identity. The overman cannot function simply as another transcendent world. Recurrence must intensify rather than evade temporality. Zarathustra must both teach and overcome dependence upon being a teacher. Negation must become capable of yielding creation rather than endless destruction.\n\nThese constraints materially narrow viable constructions and interact across the completed work.\n\nThat securely establishes **7: advanced constraint coordination** and moves toward 8.\n\nI stop at 7.5 because substantial local flexibility remains. Individual speeches, figures, parables, characters, and even some conceptual formulations could be changed without destroying the central operation. The protocol requires CD to track narrowing of the viable solution space rather than complexity or density of allusion. \n\n**Principal evidence:** the requirement to construct affirmation without undoing the prior critique of transcendence, morality, temporality, and reactive negation.\n\n### **ID — Inferential Distance: 8.2**\n\nSeveral governing transitions are highly non-routine:\n\n**collapse of externally guaranteed values → not resignation but value creation;**\n\n**freedom-from → insufficient without freedom-for;**\n\n**overcoming inherited valuation → necessity of overcoming the overcoming self;**\n\n**irreversibility of the past → problem of revenge against time → radical affirmation;**\n\n**suffering → neither straightforward condemnation nor justification → incorporation into an affirmative relation toward becoming.**\n\nThe inferential distance is heightened because the artifact repeatedly refuses conventional argumentative exposition and instead develops relations through narrative recurrence, transformation, symbolic juxtaposition, and conceptual reversal.\n\nThis fully establishes **8: deep inferential transition**.\n\nI stop at 8.2 because some major transitions are proclaimed or poetically enacted more strongly than they are inferentially reconstructed. Under the protocol, the magnitude of a leap cannot substitute for demonstrated inference. \n\n**Principal evidence:** the reconstruction of nihilism into self-overcoming and then of self-overcoming into affirmation of recurrence/becoming.\n\n### **IC — Integrative Compression: 8.5**\n\nA relatively compact architecture—\n\n**inheritance → negation → self-overcoming → creation → recursive overcoming → affirmation**\n\n—organizes a remarkably heterogeneous field: morality, religion, psychology, culture, temporality, embodiment, suffering, education, solitude, friendship, politics, aspiration, meaning, and death.\n\nThe recurring symbolic oppositions achieve further compression:\n\n**gravity / dance**\n\n**revenge / affirmation**\n\n**camel / lion / child**\n\n**descent / ascent**\n\n**last man / overman**\n\n**fragment / recurrence**\n\nThese structures preserve substantial distinctions while making apparently separate episodes mutually reconstructible.\n\nThat fully establishes **8-level integrative compression**, with meaningful movement toward 9.\n\nI stop at 8.5 because some of the apparent unity is interpretively reconstructed rather than explicitly constrained by the artifact, and forcing every episode into a single architecture would violate the protocol's Projection Independence safeguard.\n\n**Principal evidence:** the self-overcoming/affirmation architecture organizing philosophical, psychological, narrative, existential, and symbolic material simultaneously.\n\n### **GR — Generalization Reach: 7.7**\n\nThe underlying structures transfer successfully across numerous substantially different cases.\n\nSelf-overcoming operates across morality, personal identity, teaching, cultural creation, knowledge, psychological development, and Zarathustra's own trajectory. The creation/negation relation transfers across inherited morality, personal transformation, cultural criticism, and existential orientation. Affirmation is tested against suffering, temporality, solitude, desire, mortality, and recurrence.\n\nThis securely establishes **7-level high transfer** and approaches 8.\n\nI keep it below 8 because much of the demonstrated transfer remains within interrelated human, psychological, cultural, ethical, and existential problem-spaces. The work suggests dramatically wider reach, but the protocol prohibits converting universal philosophical aspiration into demonstrated structural transfer. \n\n**Principal evidence:** preservation of self-overcoming and affirmation structures across ethical, psychological, cultural, interpersonal, temporal, and existential contexts.\n\n---\n\n### Committed profile\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 8.0 / 8.6 / 7.5 / 8.2 / 8.5 / 7.7**\n\nProfile locked.\n\nThe profile's strongest features are **Abstraction Depth** and **Integrative Compression**. Its relative limitation is Constraint Density: the artifact's aphoristic, poetic, and polysemous construction creates more legitimate structural freedom than a tightly deductive system would permit. That flexibility should not be mistaken for either greater or lesser intelligence; it affects specifically the dimension whose criterion is restriction of viable constructions.\n\nFollowing the protocol, the scores are committed independently before aggregation rather than modified to produce a desired total. \n\n8.0+8.6+7.5+8.2+8.5+7.76=48.56=8.0833…\\frac{8.0+8.6+7.5+8.2+8.5+7.7}{6} = \\frac{48.5}{6} = 8.0833\\ldots \n\n**CMS = 808**\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 808**\n\nRL: 8.0\n\nAD: 8.6\n\nCD: 7.5\n\nID: 8.2\n\nIC: 8.5\n\nGR: 7.7\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The 3b/3c boundary. The artifact unmistakably performs fractured recursive confrontation, while 3c depends on whether eternal recurrence, self-overcoming, and affirmation together constitute a successfully achieved existential integration rather than an extraordinarily powerful demand for integration. On the completed artifact, the recurring transformation from negation toward affirmation is sufficient for 3c, but this is the classification's closest boundary.", "## Operational Order (TORC): **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is best classified as **3c**.\n\nIts dominant operation is neither simple symbolic representation nor merely the exposure of existential fracture. The work takes a world in which inherited metaphysical and moral guarantees have lost authority—most famously through the “death of God”—and asks how consciousness can nevertheless affirm existence without restoring those guarantees. Its central movement is therefore **integration after fracture**: mortality, suffering, contingency, recurrence, solitude, failed discipleship, self-overcoming, and the instability of values are not eliminated but incorporated into an affirmative existential orientation.\n\nThat is precisely the distinguishing operation of 3c. Under the protocol, 3c requires the contradiction to remain real while consciousness develops a coherent orientation capable of containing it; optimism, redemption, or spiritual imagery alone do not suffice. \n\nThe decisive structures are the **death of transcendent foundations**, **self-overcoming**, the **Übermensch**, the transformation of values, the repeated movement through solitude and return, and above all **eternal recurrence** as an extreme test of affirmation. Zarathustra's task is not to demonstrate that suffering or finitude can be removed. It is to formulate a mode of existence capable of saying yes to becoming, including its recurrence.\n\nThe work therefore goes beyond 3b confrontation. It attempts to transform existential fracture into a coherent mode of inhabiting reality.\n\n### Boundary analysis\n\n**Why 3c rather than 3b.**\n\nA 3b reading is initially very strong. The work confronts nihilism, mortality, loneliness, failed communication, resentment, the collapse of inherited value, instability of identity, and the inability of consciousness to rely on an externally guaranteed order. These are genuine consciousness–existence fractures rather than merely social defects.\n\nBut 3b is insufficient because *Zarathustra* does not remain primarily within confrontation. Its characteristic operation is to repeatedly **convert negation into orientation**:\n\n-  the death of God becomes the condition for value-creation rather than simply metaphysical loss; \n-  suffering becomes something to be incorporated into self-overcoming rather than merely endured as contradiction; \n-  becoming is affirmed instead of measured against an immutable transcendent realm; \n-  solitude becomes both danger and condition of transformation; \n-  eternal recurrence radicalizes finitude into a test of whether one can affirm existence without remainder. \n\nThe protocol defines the 3b→3c transition exactly this way: 3c preserves the fracture but adds a coherent existential structure capable of containing it. \n\nThe novel-philosophical form matters here. Zarathustra repeatedly fails, misunderstands himself, retreats, returns, confronts disgust, pity, longing, and inadequacy. The achieved orientation is therefore not naïve triumphalism. Affirmation must contain the very conditions that make affirmation difficult.\n\n**Why not G.**\n\nThis is the crucial upper boundary.\n\nThe work contains several ideas that can **look generative**: will to power, genealogy-like accounts of valuation, self-overcoming, resentment, the Übermensch, and eternal recurrence. These can organize large regions of psychology, morality, culture, and existential life.\n\nBut TORC requires something stronger than a powerful philosophical worldview. G requires a newly disclosed generative structure that relocates the explanatory foundation of an **independently identifiable target domain**, making lower-order explanation insufficient. \n\n*Zarathustra* does not establish one such mechanism with sufficient explanatory discipline. “Will to power,” for example, is not developed here into a sufficiently constrained generative mechanism capable of explaining why independently given phenomena assume their specific forms. Eternal recurrence functions principally as an existential and evaluative test; the Übermensch functions as an orienting horizon; self-overcoming provides a dynamic of transformation. Together they form an extraordinarily powerful **integrated existential architecture**, but they do not cross the protocol's explanatory-relocation threshold.\n\nThat distinction matters because TORC explicitly warns that large, universal, or philosophically ambitious structures are not automatically generative. \n\nThus **3c is sufficient; G is not demonstrated**.\n\n---\n\n# Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\nThe six dimensions are assessed independently and committed before CMS calculation, as required by the protocol. \n\n### RL — Relational Load: **8.3**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe work maintains dense relations among nihilism, value, overcoming, resentment, pity, body, spirit, solitude, discipleship, recurrence, temporality, creation, destruction, suffering, affirmation, hierarchy, becoming, morality, and identity.\n\nThese relations are strongly nonlocal. Eternal recurrence modifies the significance of affirmation; the death of God changes the status of value-creation; self-overcoming connects personal transformation to moral critique; Zarathustra's failures as teacher recursively affect the meaning of his doctrines.\n\nThis satisfies the 8-level condition of dense cross-structural dependency.\n\nMovement toward 9 is real because the relations span psychological, ethical, metaphysical, rhetorical, narrative, and existential levels. But they are not uniformly mutually constraining enough across the whole artifact to establish complete 9-level heterogeneous interdependence.\n\n**Principal evidence:** the reciprocal dependence of death-of-God, nihilism, value-creation, self-overcoming, recurrence, suffering, and affirmation.\n\n### AD — Abstraction Depth: **8.8**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe artifact moves from concrete images, speeches, encounters, bodily metaphors, animals, landscapes, and interpersonal episodes into highly abstract structures concerning valuation, temporality, becoming, subjectivity, morality, self-transformation, and affirmation.\n\nMore importantly, it repeatedly makes the conditions of valuation themselves objects of reflection. It does not simply ask which values are correct; it asks what kinds of life produce values, what relation values have to strength or resentment, and whether consciousness can create rather than inherit its evaluative horizon.\n\nThat securely establishes deep constrained abstraction at 8 and approaches 9.\n\nThe remaining shortfall is that the work's highest abstractions are deliberately poetic, polysemous, and resistant to a single invariant architecture. That fecundity contributes to the work's power but prevents the unusually disciplined relation-preservation required by full 9.\n\n**Principal evidence:** movement from concrete moral claims → genealogy of valuing → self-overcoming → meta-level inquiry into the creation and affirmation of values themselves.\n\n### CD — Constraint Density: **7.6**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 7–8.**\n\nThe artifact must maintain a difficult set of simultaneous requirements: reject transcendent guarantees without collapsing into nihilism; affirm becoming without treating suffering as unreal; advocate self-overcoming without fixing a final static self; create values without simply reinstating dogma; use Zarathustra as teacher while repeatedly undermining discipleship and imitation.\n\nThese constraints interact significantly. Solving one too simply damages another. A purely consolatory ending would undercut recurrence; a fixed doctrine would contradict self-overcoming; simple optimism would trivialize nihilism.\n\nThat fully clears 7 and moves substantially toward 8.\n\nThe 8 anchor is not fully satisfied because the work's aphoristic, poetic, and episodic form permits considerable local variation. Individual speeches or episodes could be removed or rearranged without collapsing the core achievement.\n\n**Principal evidence:** simultaneous maintenance of anti-nihilism, anti-dogmatism, self-overcoming, affirmation, suffering, and pedagogical self-critique.\n\n### ID — Inferential Distance: **8.3**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nSeveral of the work's central transitions are deeply non-routine:\n\nthe collapse of inherited value → not despair but creation;\n\nsuffering → not merely evil but material for transformation;\n\nbecoming → not deficiency relative to permanence but something affirmable;\n\nthe highest affirmation → willingness to affirm the recurrence of the entire life, not only selected parts.\n\nThese are genuine restructurings of the problem-space rather than incremental philosophical deductions.\n\nThe complete 8 anchor is therefore met.\n\nMovement toward 9 comes from the underdetermined leap from nihilism to affirmative self-overcoming: many alternative responses are possible, and Zarathustra's architecture is far from obvious.\n\nI stop at 8.3 because many transitions are enacted rhetorically, poetically, or experimentally rather than demonstrated through exceptionally tight inferential reconstruction.\n\n**Principal evidence:** transformation of nihilism into value-creation and eternal recurrence into a criterion of radical affirmation.\n\n### IC — Integrative Compression: **8.5**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nA relatively compact architecture—**death of inherited transcendence → nihilistic crisis → self-overcoming/value-creation → affirmation of becoming → recurrence as maximal test**—organizes a large heterogeneous body of material.\n\nThat architecture connects religion, morality, psychology, temporality, suffering, education, politics, embodiment, solitude, creativity, resentment, and identity.\n\nThis fully satisfies very high integrative compression.\n\nThere is substantial movement toward 9 because a small number of recurrent structures continually reconstruct apparently disparate episodes and doctrines. Yet the work deliberately refuses complete systematization. Its symbols preserve multiple partially incompatible meanings, and not every major strand is derivable from one economical core.\n\n**Principal evidence:** the same architecture explaining religious critique, moral transformation, psychology of resentment, selfhood, temporality, and existential affirmation.\n\n### GR — Generalization Reach: **8.0**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe underlying structures transfer across markedly different cases while preserving recognizable identity. Self-overcoming applies to individuals, values, cultural forms, identities, and modes of thought. Ressentiment-related dynamics transfer across morality, interpersonal psychology, religion, and culture. Affirmation versus negation operates across suffering, temporality, desire, morality, and selfhood.\n\nThat reaches the 8 anchor.\n\nI do not move significantly toward 9 because the transfer remains concentrated within interconnected domains of human valuation, culture, psychology, ethics, and existential orientation. The artifact does not demonstrate equally disciplined structural portability across exceptionally heterogeneous domains.\n\n**Principal evidence:** transfer of self-overcoming, valuation, resentment, and affirmation across psychology, morality, religion, culture, temporality, and identity.\n\n### Committed profile\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 8.3 / 8.8 / 7.6 / 8.3 / 8.5 / 8.0**\n\n**Profile locked.**\n\nCMS is mechanically derived only after commitment; the protocol gives all six dimensions equal weight. \n\n8.3+8.8+7.6+8.3+8.5+8.06=8.25\\frac{8.3+8.8+7.6+8.3+8.5+8.0}{6} = 8.25 \n\n**CMS = 825**\n\nThe profile is strongest in **AD and IC**: the work moves through deep layers of meta-valuation while organizing a very broad existential field through a comparatively compact architecture. CD is the relative bottleneck because its poetic and episodic mode deliberately permits multiplicity, ambiguity, and local independence rather than enforcing a narrowly constrained systematic construction.\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 825**\n\nRL: 8.3\n\nAD: 8.8\n\nCD: 7.6\n\nID: 8.3\n\nIC: 8.5\n\nGR: 8.0\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The main uncertainty is the 3c/G boundary: structures such as self-overcoming, ressentiment, and will-to-power-like dynamics have genuine explanatory reach, but in *Thus Spoke Zarathustra* they are not established with enough independently constrained generative specificity to require explanatory relocation rather than integrated recursive interpretation.", "## Operational Order (TORC): **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is best classified as **3c**.\n\nIts dominant operation is not adequately captured by symbolic organization alone. The work repeatedly turns consciousness back upon inherited morality, metaphysics, religion, pity, ressentiment, nihilism, selfhood, value, suffering, and recurrence, asking not merely what these structures mean but **how a human being can remain coherent after the collapse of inherited grounds of meaning**.\n\nThat places the work securely inside the recursive family. More specifically, its dominant movement is toward **integration**: suffering, finitude, contradiction, loss of transcendent guarantees, and the destabilization of inherited value are not simply confronted. They are reorganized into an existential orientation centered on self-overcoming, value-creation, affirmation, and ultimately the demand to affirm becoming rather than escape it.\n\nUnder the protocol, 3c requires preservation of existential contradiction together with a coherent orientation capable of containing it; mere consolation or optimism is insufficient. \n\n### Boundary analysis\n\n**Why 3c rather than 3b.** The work plainly satisfies the underlying 3b condition: its principal fracture is not merely social or institutional. The collapse of divine/metaphysical guarantees, the instability of inherited morality, the problem of nihilism, and the tension between becoming and the demand for permanence all operate at the level of consciousness’s relation to existence itself.\n\nThat is 3b territory. The protocol defines 3b as confrontation with an existential contradiction that cannot simply be repaired through better institutions, morality, politics, or behavior. \n\nBut 3b is not sufficient because the work does not remain at confrontation. Zarathustra develops a positive existential architecture: self-overcoming rather than preservation, creation rather than obedience to inherited values, affirmation rather than ressentiment, and recurrence as a test of whether existence can be affirmed without appeal to another world.\n\nThe contradiction is not erased. Becoming remains becoming; suffering remains real; mortality is not canceled; certainty is not restored. Yet the work attempts to construct a coherent way of inhabiting those conditions. That is exactly what distinguishes 3c from 3b.\n\n**Integration Resistance test: passed.** The book’s affirmative movement is not simply emotional uplift. Its “yes” to life depends on retaining the very instability, suffering, finitude, and lack of transcendent guarantee that produced the crisis in the first place. The protocol’s requirement that contradiction remain operative is therefore met. \n\n**Why not Level 2.** Symbolism is pervasive—mountains, animals, sun, descent, dance, child, lion, serpent, dwarf, bridge, overman—but symbolic interpretation alone does not explain the completed artifact. The work continually reflects on the conditions under which values, selves, meanings, and world-interpretations are produced and transformed. Representation itself becomes an object of inquiry.\n\nThat exceeds symbolic consciousness.\n\n### Why not G\n\nThe strongest candidate for G is the work’s genealogy-like relocation of value: values are not treated as eternally given truths but as humanly generated evaluations tied to forms of life, drives, strength, weakness, ressentiment, overcoming, and interpretation.\n\nHowever, the protocol’s G threshold is stricter than radical philosophy. G requires a newly disclosed generative structure that **replaces** the previously sufficient explanatory foundation and generates nontrivial explanatory consequences across an independently identifiable target. \n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* approaches that threshold but does not clear it securely. Its claims concerning will, overcoming, recurrence, value-creation, higher and lower forms of life, and affirmation function partly as aphoristic, poetic, prophetic, and symbolic orientation rather than as a sufficiently articulated generative mechanism that explains why otherwise distinct phenomena take the specific forms they do.\n\nIn protocol terms, the text does more than merely present a worldview, but its dominant successful operation remains the recursive integration of nihilistic and existential fracture. A G reading requires importing a more systematic Nietzschean explanatory architecture than this artifact alone compels.\n\nSo the lowest sufficient classification remains **3c**.\n\n---\n\n# Cognitive Magnitude Score\n\nIndependent dimensional commitment:\n\n**RL 8.3 / AD 9.0 / CD 7.6 / ID 8.6 / IC 8.7 / GR 8.1**\n\nThe protocol requires each decimal score to be anchored between adjacent integer definitions, with 9.x permitted only where the complete 9 anchor is demonstrated. \n\n### RL — Relational Load: **8.3**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe work coordinates numerous nonlocal relations among nihilism, morality, religion, pity, ressentiment, self-overcoming, value-creation, strength, weakness, solitude, community, recurrence, temporality, suffering, affirmation, and the figure of the overman.\n\nThese relations materially constrain one another. Self-overcoming is unintelligible without the critique of fixed identity; value-creation depends on the collapse of inherited valuation; affirmation depends on recurrence and becoming; the overman functions relative to these same structures rather than as an isolated symbol.\n\nThat fully satisfies RL8, where remote relations materially constrain one another and simultaneous coordination is central. \n\nI stop below RL9 because the relational field, though dense, remains comparatively homogeneous around existential, evaluative, psychological, and metaphysical concerns rather than spanning exceptionally heterogeneous domains.\n\n**Principal evidence:** sustained coupling among nihilism, valuation, selfhood, suffering, becoming, overcoming, recurrence, and affirmation.\n\n### AD — Abstraction Depth: **9.0**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 9–10.**\n\nThe complete AD9 anchor is warranted.\n\nThe work moves from concrete moral and psychological phenomena to increasingly abstract structures: inherited values → valuation itself → conditions of value-creation → self-overcoming → becoming → affirmation of existence as such. It then recursively interrogates the desire for permanence, transcendence, and metaphysical stability.\n\nIts deepest abstraction is not simply “life” or “will,” but the relation between beings that evaluate and the processes through which value and identity become constituted.\n\nThat is exceptional meta-representational depth with strong preservation across levels.\n\nI assign 9.0 rather than movement toward 10 because the abstraction architecture is intentionally poetic and plural rather than maximally explicit or formally disciplined.\n\n**Principal evidence:** recursive movement from moral judgments to the production of values, and from particular suffering to the conditions under which becoming itself can be affirmed.\n\n### CD — Constraint Density: **7.6**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 7–8.**\n\nThe work must keep several demanding tensions simultaneously viable: affirmation cannot collapse into simple optimism; self-overcoming cannot become mere egoism; value-creation must avoid reinstating the transcendent foundations it rejects; critique of pity must remain distinct from simple cruelty; recurrence must function as more than cosmological decoration; overman must remain connected to transformation rather than merely superiority.\n\nThis establishes CD7 and moves substantially toward CD8.\n\nI stop below 8 because the text’s aphoristic and prophetic form gives it considerable interpretive flexibility. Many formulations can coexist without being forced into a narrowly constrained systematic structure.\n\n**Principal evidence:** interacting requirements linking nihilism, valuation, affirmation, recurrence, overcoming, and critique of inherited morality.\n\n### ID — Inferential Distance: **8.6**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe work repeatedly makes highly non-routine inferential transitions:\n\n-  from the collapse of inherited values to the necessity of creating values; \n-  from suffering to the possibility of affirmation rather than escape; \n-  from identity to self-overcoming; \n-  from morality to valuation as an expression of forms of life; \n-  from recurrence to a test of whether existence can be affirmed without remainder. \n\nThese are major restructurings rather than routine deductions, satisfying ID8.\n\nThe work approaches ID9 because the relevant phenomena substantially underdetermine the successful reconstruction: the move from nihilism to affirmative value-creation is far from obvious. But I stop short of 9 because many crucial transitions are proclaimed, dramatized, or symbolically staged rather than inferentially reconstructed with the degree of constraint demanded by the full 9 anchor. \n\n**Principal evidence:** transformation of nihilism from a terminal condition into the precondition for self-overcoming and affirmative valuation.\n\n### IC — Integrative Compression: **8.7**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nA relatively compact architecture—\n\n**collapse of inherited value → nihilism → self-overcoming → creation of value → affirmation of becoming**\n\n—organizes a large heterogeneous field of moral, psychological, religious, existential, and metaphysical phenomena.\n\nThe architecture also has strong reconstructive power: pity, resentment, ascetic longing, the desire for permanence, loneliness, domination, creativity, suffering, and recurrence become intelligible as different expressions or tests within that framework.\n\nThis fully satisfies IC8 and approaches IC9. The protocol reserves IC9 for remarkably economical organization of very large heterogeneous complexity with unusually fine preservation. \n\nI stop at 8.7 because the text’s plurality resists reduction to one compact mechanism without interpretive loss.\n\n**Principal evidence:** a small set of relations concerning nihilism, overcoming, valuation, and affirmation organizes much of the book’s symbolic and philosophical diversity.\n\n### GR — Generalization Reach: **8.1**\n\n**Bounding anchors: 8–9.**\n\nThe transferable structure is clear: inherited frameworks can cease to command belief; agents then confront a crisis of valuation; responses can take the form of resentment, retreat, passive nihilism, or active revaluation; coherent transformation requires creation and affirmation rather than mere negation.\n\nThat architecture transfers across moral systems, religious commitments, identity formation, artistic creation, personal development, cultural transition, and political or social value-conflict.\n\nThis satisfies GR8.\n\nI assign only slight movement toward 9 because the protocol requires very distant problem-spaces for exceptional generalization. The artifact’s strongest transfers remain within human evaluative, psychological, cultural, and existential domains.\n\n**Principal evidence:** preservation of the same valuation/nihilism/overcoming structure across individual, moral, religious, and cultural contexts.\n\n---\n\nThe profile is committed and locked:\n\n**RL / AD / CD / ID / IC / GR: 8.3 / 9.0 / 7.6 / 8.6 / 8.7 / 8.1**\n\nSum = **50.3**\n\nMean = **8.3833…**\n\n**CMS = 838**\n\nThe CMS is calculated mechanically from the six committed decimal scores using equal weighting, mean × 100, rounded to the nearest whole integer. \n\nThe profile is strongest in **Abstraction Depth** and **Integrative Compression**, with high Inferential Distance. Constraint Density is the relative bottleneck because the artifact achieves its operation through a deliberately open, poetic, aphoristic structure rather than a tightly closed systematic argument.\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)**\n\n**3c | 838**\n\nRL: 8.3\n\nAD: 9.0\n\nCD: 7.6\n\nID: 8.6\n\nIC: 8.7\n\nGR: 8.1\n\n**Confidence:** Moderate\n\n**Primary uncertainty:** The 3c/G boundary. The work clearly relocates the *question* of value from transcendent givenness toward valuation, creation, and forms of life, but the artifact alone does not articulate that relocation as a sufficiently constrained generative mechanism to make G the lowest sufficient explanation rather than an exceptionally deep integrated recursive operation."];
export const consensusReport="The seven reports show **complete TORC convergence**: every evaluator independently assigns *Thus Spoke Zarathustra* **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**. The numerical profiles also share a clear common shape—very high abstraction depth and integrative compression, high inferential distance, and comparatively lower constraint density—with the principal residual uncertainty concentrated at the **3c → G boundary**.\n\n## 1. Seven evaluator results\n\n| EvaluatorTORCCMSRLADCDIDICGRConfidence |    |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |          |\n| -------------------------------------- | -- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | -------- |\n| 1                                      | 3c | 795 | 7.4 | 8.8 | 6.8 | 8.2 | 8.4 | 8.1 | High     |\n| 2                                      | 3c | 853 | 8.5 | 9.0 | 8.0 | 8.7 | 9.0 | 8.0 | Moderate |\n| 3                                      | 3c | 813 | 8.3 | 8.8 | 7.5 | 8.2 | 8.5 | 7.5 | Moderate |\n| 4                                      | 3c | 842 | 8.4 | 9.0 | 8.0 | 8.4 | 8.7 | 8.0 | Moderate |\n| 5                                      | 3c | 808 | 8.0 | 8.6 | 7.5 | 8.2 | 8.5 | 7.7 | Moderate |\n| 6                                      | 3c | 825 | 8.3 | 8.8 | 7.6 | 8.3 | 8.5 | 8.0 | Moderate |\n| 7                                      | 3c | 838 | 8.3 | 9.0 | 7.6 | 8.6 | 8.7 | 8.1 | Moderate |\n\nEvaluator 1 reports **3c | 795** with profile 7.4 / 8.8 / 6.8 / 8.2 / 8.4 / 8.1 and High confidence.  Evaluator 2 reports **3c | 853** with 8.5 / 9.0 / 8.0 / 8.7 / 9.0 / 8.0 and Moderate confidence.  Evaluator 3 reports **3c | 813** with 8.3 / 8.8 / 7.5 / 8.2 / 8.5 / 7.5 and Moderate confidence. \n\nEvaluator 4 reports **3c | 842** with 8.4 / 9.0 / 8.0 / 8.4 / 8.7 / 8.0 and Moderate confidence.  Evaluator 5 reports **3c | 808** with 8.0 / 8.6 / 7.5 / 8.2 / 8.5 / 7.7 and Moderate confidence.  Evaluator 6 reports **3c | 825** with 8.3 / 8.8 / 7.6 / 8.3 / 8.5 / 8.0 and Moderate confidence.  Evaluator 7 reports **3c | 838** with 8.3 / 9.0 / 7.6 / 8.6 / 8.7 / 8.1 and Moderate confidence. \n\n## 2. Numerical aggregation\n\nUsing population standard deviation across the complete seven-evaluator set:\n\n| MeasureMeanMedianMinimumMaximumRangeSD |           |         |     |     |     |      |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | --- | --- | --- | ---- |\n| **CMS**                                | **824.9** | **825** | 795 | 853 | 58  | 19.2 |\n| **RL**                                 | 8.2       | **8.3** | 7.4 | 8.5 | 1.1 | 0.3  |\n| **AD**                                 | 8.9       | **8.8** | 8.6 | 9.0 | 0.4 | 0.1  |\n| **CD**                                 | 7.6       | **7.6** | 6.8 | 8.0 | 1.2 | 0.4  |\n| **ID**                                 | 8.4       | **8.3** | 8.2 | 8.7 | 0.5 | 0.2  |\n| **IC**                                 | 8.6       | **8.5** | 8.4 | 9.0 | 0.6 | 0.2  |\n| **GR**                                 | 7.9       | **8.0** | 7.5 | 8.1 | 0.6 | 0.2  |\n\nThe median dimensional values are used below as the consensus profile.\n\n## 3. TORC consensus\n\nEvaluator classifications: **3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c**.\n\nFrequency: **3c — 7/7 (100%)**.\n\nModal classification: **3c**.\n\n**Consensus TORC: 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness.**\n\n**TORC agreement: High / unanimous.**\n\nThe reports repeatedly distinguish 3c from 3b through the same operation: existential contradiction is **preserved**, but the artifact develops an affirmative orientation capable of containing it. Becoming, suffering, contingency, mortality, nihilism, instability of value, and recurrence are not abolished. Instead, self-overcoming, value creation, affirmation, and recurrence reorganize consciousness’s relation to those conditions.   \n\nThere is therefore **no TORC classification disagreement**. Six evaluators nevertheless identify the **3c/G boundary** as their principal uncertainty, while one identifies 3b/3c as closest. The recurrent G question is whether the work’s account of valuation, nihilism, self-overcoming, and value creation becomes a sufficiently constrained mechanism that **relocates the explanatory foundation** of an independently identifiable target domain. The reports consistently answer no: those structures possess major explanatory power, but the completed artifact is more securely characterized as recursive existential transformation and integration than as generative explanatory relocation.  \n\n## 4. Consensus analysis\n\n### A. Operational Order rationale\n\nAcross all seven reports, the artifact’s dominant operation is described as **integration after existential fracture**.\n\nThe reports agree that symbolic organization alone is insufficient. The mountain and descent, metamorphoses, recurrence, overman, animals, teaching, solitude, return, and other recurring structures matter because they participate in a recursive transformation of the consciousness producing and inhabiting values. Zarathustra does not simply announce doctrines from a stable standpoint; his own failures, attachments, solitude, disgust, teaching, transformation, and capacity to bear his doctrines become part of the operation.  \n\nThe existential fracture is likewise not treated as merely social or institutionally reparable. The collapse of inherited value, becoming, suffering, temporality, mortality, and the difficulty of affirmation persist beyond any particular cultural arrangement.\n\nWhat moves the artifact from 3b to 3c is the recurrent construction of a positive orientation: **self-overcoming rather than static preservation, creation rather than inherited obedience, and affirmation rather than escape from becoming**. Eternal recurrence repeatedly appears in the reports as the hardest integration test because affirmation must encompass rather than selectively remove the resistant conditions of existence. \n\n### B. Boundary analysis\n\n**Why 3c is satisfied.** All seven evaluators find both components required for integration: the underlying contradiction remains operative, and a coherent orientation develops within it. Self-overcoming does not produce a final immutable self; value creation does not restore an external metaphysical guarantor; affirmation does not remove suffering or becoming; recurrence intensifies rather than dissolves the problem.\n\nThe repeated camel → lion → child architecture captures the same transition in compressed form: inherited burden is followed by negation, but negation itself proves insufficient and must become creative affirmation. Zarathustra’s own recursive transformation prevents the resulting orientation from functioning simply as a proposition externally announced.\n\n**Why G is not satisfied.** The evaluators repeatedly acknowledge a plausible G candidate: human valuation and nihilism after the collapse of transcendent foundations, organized through self-overcoming, value creation, resentment, forms of life, affirmation, or related structures.\n\nThe shared limiting argument is **explanatory replacement**. The completed artifact does not establish those structures as a sufficiently constrained generative mechanism explaining why independently identifiable phenomena take their particular forms such that 3c becomes inadequate. Rather, the concepts operate principally through prophetic speech, symbolism, existential enactment, recursive testing, and philosophical reorientation.  \n\nThe one evaluator whose primary uncertainty lies downward at **3b/3c** accepts 3c because the recurrent movement from negation toward affirmation is sufficiently achieved, but questions whether recurrence, self-overcoming, and affirmation constitute accomplished integration rather than primarily a demand for integration.  This is a material nuance, but not a classificatory split.\n\n## 5. Six-dimensional synthesis\n\n**RL — Relational Load: 8.3 consensus; range 7.4–8.5.** The reports identify consequential relations among nihilism, inherited value, value creation, self-overcoming, recurrence, suffering, temporality, resentment, pity, solitude, teaching, discipleship, identity, embodiment, and affirmation. Earlier doctrines are qualified by Zarathustra’s subsequent development, and recurrence alters the meaning of affirmation. The disagreement concerns how globally interdependent the episodic architecture is: higher scorers see dense cross-structural dependency, while the lowest evaluator emphasizes the relative detachability of many speeches and episodes.  \n\n**AD — Abstraction Depth: 8.8 consensus; range 8.6–9.0.** This is the most stable major strength. Concrete images and moral phenomena repeatedly ascend into structures of valuation, the production of values, self-transformation, temporality, becoming, and affirmation. Several reports stress the meta-level movement from asking which values are valid to asking how valuation itself is produced and how the valuating consciousness must transform. The only disagreement is whether the poetic and polyvalent architecture fully clears 9 or sits immediately below it.  \n\n**CD — Constraint Density: 7.6 consensus; range 6.8–8.0.** This is the largest numerical spread. Evaluators agree that the artifact must simultaneously avoid several collapses: affirmation cannot become consolation, value creation cannot reinstall transcendent authority, self-overcoming cannot terminate in a static self, and negation must become creation rather than endless destruction. Higher scorers see these philosophical, narrative, psychological, and rhetorical constraints as sufficiently cross-coupled for 8; lower scorers emphasize the considerable freedom permitted by the aphoristic and poetic form.  \n\n**ID — Inferential Distance: 8.3 consensus; range 8.2–8.7.** The reports converge on several strongly non-routine transitions: collapse of inherited value → creation rather than skepticism; freedom-from → creative freedom-to; suffering → material for affirmation rather than simple objection; identity → self-overcoming; recurrence → maximal test of affirmation. The shared ceiling comes from the way many of these transitions are dramatized, proclaimed, symbolized, or rhetorically enacted rather than derived through an exceptionally constrained evidential route.  \n\n**IC — Integrative Compression: 8.5 consensus; range 8.4–9.0.** Along with AD, this is a recurring profile strength. A small family of structures—self-overcoming, creation, becoming, affirmation, recurrence, and related value dynamics—organizes a broad field of morality, psychology, religion, temporality, suffering, culture, identity, embodiment, pedagogy, and existential orientation. Higher scorers judge this sufficient for 9-level compression; lower scorers emphasize that substantial symbolic plurality remains irreducible and should not be forced into a single architecture.  \n\n**GR — Generalization Reach: 8.0 consensus; range 7.5–8.1.** The underlying structures transfer across morality, religion, personal identity, education, artistic creation, cultural criticism, psychological development, suffering, interpersonal relations, and existential agency. Self-overcoming is repeatedly cited as a particularly clear transferable invariant. The recurrent ceiling is domain distance: all evaluators resist converting broad applicability across human existential and cultural life into evidence of transfer across exceptionally distant problem-spaces.  \n\n## 6. Final CMS\n\n**Mean CMS: 824.9**\n\n**Median CMS: 825**\n\nThe headline consensus CMS is therefore **825**.\n\nThe evaluator CMS values are **795, 853, 813, 842, 808, 825, 838**. No value has been removed or adjusted.\n\n## 7. Evaluator agreement\n\n**TORC agreement: High.** All seven independently assign 3c.\n\n**CMS stability: High.** Scores range from 795 to 853, with a population SD of 19.2 around a mean of 824.9. Despite different interpolation judgments, the overall magnitude assessment is tightly clustered.\n\n**Dimensional stability: Moderate.** The profile shape is highly consistent, especially for AD, ID, IC, and GR, but RL ranges by 1.1 points and CD by 1.2. The largest disagreement is therefore **Constraint Density**, driven by differing judgments about how tightly the artifact’s philosophical requirements constrain its deliberately poetic, aphoristic, episodic construction.\n\nThe largest operational uncertainty is different: although nobody actually assigns G, six reports identify **3c/G** as the principal boundary question because self-overcoming and value creation have genuine explanatory reach but are judged insufficiently constrained to require explanatory relocation.\n\n# Demonstrated Intelligence Profile (DIP)\n\n**3c | 825**\n\n**Mean CMS:** 824.9\n\n**Median CMS:** 825\n\n**RL:** 8.3\n\n**AD:** 8.8\n\n**CD:** 7.6\n\n**ID:** 8.3\n\n**IC:** 8.5\n\n**GR:** 8.0\n\n**TORC agreement:** High\n\n**CMS stability:** High\n\n**Dimensional stability:** Moderate\n\n**Evaluator distribution:** 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c, 3c\n\n**Primary point of disagreement:** The largest substantive uncertainty is whether the artifact’s self-overcoming/value-creation architecture becomes a sufficiently constrained explanatory mechanism to cross from integrated recursive consciousness into G-level explanatory relocation; all seven ultimately conclude that it does not.\n\n# Consensus Evaluation\n\n**Friedrich Nietzsche,** ***Thus Spoke Zarathustra***\n**TORC 3c | CMS 825**\n\nAcross seven independent TORC/DIP evaluations, *Thus Spoke Zarathustra* receives a unanimous classification of **Level 3c — Integrated Recursive Consciousness**, with a median Cognitive Magnitude Score of **825** and mean CMS of **824.9**.\n\nThe evaluators converge on the same central operation. The work does not merely represent nihilism, the collapse of inherited values, suffering, mortality, becoming, solitude, or the instability of identity. Nor is its extraordinary symbolic architecture sufficient to explain what the completed artifact performs. Zarathustra himself repeatedly becomes subject to the transformations he announces: the teacher must confront his relation to disciples, the creator must overcome residual negation, and the advocate of affirmation must become capable of bearing the existential conditions his teaching demands.\n\nThe underlying fracture is therefore recursive and existential. Once inherited transcendent guarantees lose their authority, consciousness cannot simply occupy a neutral standpoint outside valuation. It must continue to value while confronting the fact that values are no longer secured by an external metaphysical order. Becoming, suffering, contingency, mortality, and irreversible time remain conditions of existence rather than problems that can simply be corrected by better institutions or doctrines.\n\nThat securely establishes the 3b substrate. What moves the completed artifact to **3c** is its sustained transition from confrontation toward integration.\n\nSelf-overcoming, value creation, affirmation, the transformation of the spirit, and eternal recurrence form a positive existential architecture. The camel–lion–child sequence is repeatedly read by the evaluators as a compressed version of this movement: inherited burden becomes negation, but negation itself proves insufficient and must become creative affirmation. Likewise, self-overcoming prevents liberation from terminating in a final static identity; an achieved form itself becomes material for further transformation.\n\nEternal recurrence supplies the strongest integration test. Its operational importance is not simply a cosmological thesis. It intensifies affirmation until consciousness must confront whether it can affirm existence together with suffering, contingency, irreversibility, and becoming rather than approving only selected portions while wishing away their conditions. The contradiction is therefore not abolished. Integration consists in transforming one’s relation to it.\n\nThis distinction is crucial. The artifact does not reach 3c because it supplies optimism, spiritual consolation, or emotional resolution. The evaluators consistently emphasize that suffering remains suffering, mortality remains real, becoming remains unstable, and transcendent certainty is not restored. The affirmative orientation has force precisely because those resistant conditions remain operative.\n\nThe upper boundary is **3c versus G**. Most evaluators identify this as the principal remaining uncertainty. *Zarathustra* contains structures with genuine explanatory reach: value creation, self-overcoming, ressentiment-related dynamics, nihilism, and the relation between inherited valuation and forms of life can organize recognizable patterns across morality, psychology, religion, culture, identity, and agency.\n\nYet the seven reports do not find that these structures cross the protocol’s stricter explanatory-relocation threshold. In the completed artifact, they function primarily through symbolic transformation, prophetic speech, dramatic enactment, existential testing, and recursive orientation. The work transforms how valuation and existence can be inhabited more securely than it establishes a constrained mechanism explaining why independently identifiable phenomena must take their particular forms. Integrated recursive consciousness therefore remains sufficient to explain the dominant achievement.\n\nThe dimensional profile strongly supports that characterization.\n\n**Relational Load (8.3)** is high because nihilism, value creation, self-overcoming, recurrence, resentment, suffering, teaching, solitude, temporality, identity, and affirmation repeatedly constrain one another. Its main limitation is the artifact’s episodic and aphoristic architecture: many speeches retain meaningful local autonomy rather than depending continuously upon every other component.\n\n**Abstraction Depth (8.8)** is one of the clearest strengths. The work moves from particular moral judgments and symbolic episodes to valuation itself, from valuation to the consciousness producing values, and from the valuating consciousness to deeper structures of self-overcoming, becoming, temporality, and affirmation. The evaluators differ only on whether the deliberately poetic and polyvalent form fully establishes the disciplined abstraction architecture required for a complete 9.\n\n**Constraint Density (7.6)** is the most numerically contested dimension. The work must preserve several difficult tensions simultaneously: creation without restored transcendence, affirmation without denial of suffering, self-overcoming without static identity, teaching without simple discipleship, and negation that becomes capable of creation. The disagreement concerns how tightly these requirements restrict the possible construction. Some evaluators give greater weight to their cross-dependence; others emphasize the considerable interpretive and structural freedom of the poetic form.\n\n**Inferential Distance (8.3)** reflects the radical restructuring required by several central transitions: nihilism becomes a precondition for creation rather than an endpoint; freedom from inherited authority becomes insufficient without creative freedom; suffering becomes something affirmation must incorporate; and recurrence becomes a test of whether one can affirm existence without remainder. These are highly non-routine transformations, although their poetic and rhetorical enactment prevents still higher inferential placement.\n\n**Integrative Compression (8.5)** is the second major profile strength. A compact family of relations involving self-overcoming, creation, affirmation, becoming, and recurrence renders a very broad field of moral, psychological, religious, temporal, cultural, and existential material mutually intelligible while preserving substantial distinctions.\n\n**Generalization Reach (8.0)** is also consistently high. The architecture transfers across moral systems, identity formation, religious inheritance, education, artistic creation, cultural transition, psychological development, suffering, and interpersonal relations. The evaluators nevertheless distinguish this strong transfer across human existential domains from evidence of portability into exceptionally distant problem-spaces.\n\nThe resulting consensus is unusually robust. All seven evaluators independently identify the same Operational Order, and the numerical profiles retain the same fundamental shape: exceptional abstraction and integration, high inferential restructuring and generalization, substantial relational coordination, and relatively lower constraint density.\n\n*Thus Spoke Zarathustra* is therefore best characterized as an artifact whose dominant achievement is not merely the destruction of inherited values, but the recursive transformation of that destruction into a mode of affirmation capable of inhabiting becoming without requiring becoming to cease.\n\n**Demonstrated Intelligence Profile: 3c | 825**";
